00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:11.210
MATT: I think one of the interesting
things is that autism is certainly

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:15.530
much more recognised now and
it's certainly recognised much

00:00:15.530 --> 00:00:17.522
more in an educational setting.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:25.799
When I was at primary school and
even at middle and high school, it

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.570
really wasn't spoken about at all.

00:00:30.259 --> 00:00:36.970
The only thing that was ever really
spoken about in terms of yeah,

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.790
educational  difficulties was dyslexia.

00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:45.890
And even that required
parents to be quite proactive.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:52.370
I had a friend who was dyslexic
at primary school and I also had a

00:00:52.370 --> 00:01:00.870
friend who was really dyslexic when
I went to university, but then the

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:11.190
children who were sort of only 10,
15 or so years younger than me were

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:13.080
starting to get diagnosed with autism.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.290
So I do think there has been a great
improvement, it's being more recognised.

00:01:18.290 --> 00:01:24.285
It is being treated more and
as I mentioned before, we are

00:01:24.285 --> 00:01:27.935
starting to recognise that it
affects women and girls as well.

00:01:28.244 --> 00:01:33.354
But that it presents in slightly
different ways because of the way

00:01:33.424 --> 00:01:41.514
they're socialised and tend to have
much more effective masking strategies.

00:01:44.774 --> 00:01:51.164
There is still, in terms of mental
health services, across the board a

00:01:51.175 --> 00:01:55.125
kind of lack of funding and a lack
of provision and that seems to be

00:01:55.125 --> 00:01:58.611
particularly the case for adults.

00:02:00.656 --> 00:02:06.075
I have a friend who a little later
than me, last couple of years,

00:02:06.855 --> 00:02:08.555
got a referral for an assessment.

00:02:09.345 --> 00:02:15.090
And the waiting list, this was with the
same service in Trafford, the waiting

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.920
list for that was initially four years.

00:02:18.610 --> 00:02:20.820
When he, he got his referral.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:23.430
Though, I believe that's come down.

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:32.900
But like I say, in Greater Manchester,
as far as I know there are two to

00:02:32.900 --> 00:02:39.300
sort of commissioning groups or
whatever they're called, that actually

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.810
do this assessment for adults.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:50.490
So that's certainly an area where things
could be, could be very much improved.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:59.130
I think  that's sort of the most important
thing that's on my mind at the moment.

